"""Which test killed each mutant in the last full run: the one `test_mutants` tries first.

label of a mutant (tests/test_mutants.py) -> id of one test. A hint is only an order: it makes the
run faster and never changes a verdict (see the docstring of tests/test_mutants.py). To refresh it,
read the lines of a full run (`just mutants`, tests/tests_mutants.txt):
`killed   <file>: <label> <- <test id> [no hint]` is the line of a mutant that has no hint yet, and
`[hint missed]` one whose hint no longer kills it. Learned from the full run of 2026-10-16 (234 mutants).
"""

